    while women who do bank tend to maintain higher balances due to
    conservative saving habits and gold-linked deposits. Weekday
    transactions reflect the working economy — salary credits, business
    payments, scheduled EMIs, and routine purchases during office hours
    dominate weekday volumes. Quantitatively, this combination is 11% more
    likely to occur together than expected by random chance (lift=1.11), and
    the pattern holds in 56% of cases where the antecedent appears
    (confidence=0.56). The rule covers 14.6% of all transactions
    (support=0.1465).

  Recommendation:
        Introduce weekday 'Salary Day' savings nudges — on common salary
    credit days (1st, 7th, 15th), auto-prompt the customer to lock a portion
    into a 7-day flexi-deposit before it's spent, converting transit
    accounts into savings vehicles.

  Rule #5
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Pattern    : location=OTHER, txn_amount_group=Micro (<100)
             → gender=M
  Support    : 0.0776 (7.76%)
  Confidence : 0.8010 (80.1%)
